instrument wingie
; wingie-proc-prism — line in taken apart in the spectrum: frozen, filtered on the keys' harmonics,
; echoed bin by bin, reduced to its tonal skeleton, and sung through a cave. Set the Line/Mic
; switch to line.
;
; every scene:
;   fader1 (Mix)     how much of the processed sound against the line (or how many partials)
;   fader2 (Decay)   how long the spectrum is held (feedback, smear, the room's tail)
;   fader3 (Volume)  the colour: how deep the filter digs, how far the echoes fan out
;   keys1            the root the spectrum is tuned to; octave1 an octave down or up
;   mode1            held: the spectrum stops and sings on (freeze)
;   left LED         the line in;  right LED  what the spectrum gives back
; Step through the scenes with a held Mode button and a tap on the other.

the held chord
--------------
; hold mode1 (or any top key) and the spectrum of that instant hangs and sings with drifting
; phases; a tap on mode2 latches it until the next tap. The held spectrum is dug into the
; harmonics of the bottom key you play, so a held noise becomes a chord. A small room under it
; feeds the freeze a little of its own tail. fader1 lets the live line seep into what is held.
the hang is specfreeze samplerate=half
the latch is flipflop
the teeth are specfilter 1 samplerate=half shape=harmonics
the oct1 is transpose
the room is reverblite 3
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> hang
mode1 keys2.gate latch -> hang.freeze
mode2.tap -> latch
fader1 -> hang.blend
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> teeth.pitch
hang -> teeth
fader3 -> teeth.shape_amount
teeth -> room
fader2 -> room.size
room -20> hang                    ; the tail into the freeze
teeth room -> guard -> out
line.both -> lights.left
latch -> lights.right

echoes that arpeggiate
----------------------
; every bin of the line in gets its own echo: low ones first, high ones later, so a chord
; becomes an arpeggio of its partials. The echo goes round through a frequency shifter, each
; pass a little higher (keys2 sets how much: C none, B the most), then is smeared. fader1 the
; echo time, fader2 the feedback, fader3 the fan; the louder you play the wider it fans.
; Hold mode1 to smear everything into a still wash; a bottom key fans it by its place (C none, B all).
the bins is spectraldelay 1 samplerate=half curve=rising
the climb is freqshift shift=0
the wash is smear samplerate=half blur=0.05
the ear is follower attack=0.01 release=0.5
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> bins ear
fader1 -> bins.time
fader2 -> bins.feedback
fader3 -> bins.spread
ear -30> bins.spread
keys1.key -50> bins.spread
bins -> climb
keys2.key -6> climb.shift
climb.up -30> bins                ; round again, a little higher
bins -> wash
mode1 -> wash.blur
wash -> guard -> out
line.both -25> out
ear -> lights.left
bins -> lights.right

the tonal skeleton
------------------
; the room taken out of the line in (fader2 up: drier than dry; down: the room poured back in),
; then only its loudest partials sung again as clean sines (fader1: 1 to 40 of them). keys1
; moves the whole skeleton, mode1 or key1 (bottom C) holds it. A sine an octave under whatever
; the line sings follows along, fader3 how loud.
the dry is deverb 1 samplerate=quarter
the bones is resynth 2 samplerate=half
the ear is pitchtrack
the shadow is sine tune=-1
the hush is vca
the level is vca
the oct1 is transpose

line.both -> dry ear
fader2 -> dry.amount
-50 -> dry.amount                 ; fader2 at the middle leaves the room as it is
dry -> bones
fader1 -> bones.partials
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> bones.pitch
mode1 key1 -> bones.freeze
ear.pitch -> shadow.pitch
shadow -> hush -> level          ; only while the line sings, and as loud as fader3
ear.gate => hush.gain
fader3 -> level.gain
bones -60> out
level -40> out
ear.confidence -> lights.left
bones -> lights.right

sung through the cave
---------------------
; the line in's spectrum laid on the phases of a Wingie cave that it rings: the cave sings
; with the line's words. Bottom keys tune the cave (and strike it), top keys strike it too.
; fader1 from the plain cave to the line through it, fader2 how long the cave rings, fader3
; smooths the cross into a vocoder with no bands. Hold mode2 for the High cave's octave.
the cave is cave 2
the cross is morph 1 samplerate=half
the oct1 is transpose
the guard is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> cave
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> cave.shift
mode2 -> cave.shift
keys1.trig keys2.trig -> cave.strike
fader2 -> cave.decay
line.both -> cross.a
cave -> cross.b
fader1 -> cross.blend
fader3 -> cross.smooth
cross -> guard -> out
cave -30> out
line.both -> lights.left
cross -> lights.right
